 collection literal.\n- **Exact equality preserved** — AST on both surviving inventory tests confirms every comparison is `Eq`, none relaxed to a subset or containment.\n- **Mutation, not inspection** — a copy of the harness is made in tmp, one thing changed, and the repository's own inventory tests are re-run against it: schema file with no manifest entry, manifest entry with no file, file removed but entry kept, entry removed but file kept, three stray-file shapes, and a bogus manifest entry that must also fail the per-schema draft-2020-12/keyword checks. A control test proves the unmutated copy passes, so each failure is attributable to the mutation.\n- **The central property, demonstrated** — a throwaway schema plus its manifest line turns the copy green (including the parametrized per-schema cases, confirmed to actually select the new name), and `diff -r` then shows `tests/` byte-identical to the shipped tree.\n- **Nothing else moved** — placeholder set is exactly the six, no `manifest_schema` key, no `{{manifest` in any prompt, no orchestration module outside `schema_validator` names the manifest, coordinator/workflows/prompts/rules/scripts and `schemas/` contents unchanged, and the implementer added no test file or test function.\n\nTwo of my initial checks were over-broad — they flagged legitimate per-prompt schema references in `test_context_assembler.py` and prose mentions in `test_story_011_validation.py` as second inventories. I raised the threshold to 4-of-6 names in one collection (a claim to be *the* inventory) and made the whole-tree scan structural rather than substring-based, with the reasoning recorded in the file.","ttft_ms":2074,"ttft_stream_ms":1247,"time_to_request_ms":47,"type":"result","duration_ms":294165,"uuid":"6e2ba4eb-576b-4b45-a0f4-69edc5088940"}

